course: dictionary
lesson: 12963
title: Executed: carried out, done, or run
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Executed is a word with more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one. Usually it means carried out or done well, as in «The gymnast executed a perfect somersault.» The gymnast did the somersault properly, from start to finish.
explain: Look at what is done. «The computer executes the program when you click play» is about a computer running code. «The contract was executed when both people signed it» is about making a paper official. Each time, the words around executed show you the meaning.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. Does «The gymnast carried out a perfect somersault» still make sense? Yes, so carried out is a good meaning. If the sentence does not fit, try another meaning.
fact: «Executed» means carried out or done, especially in a complete and skilful way.
fact: In computing, a program is executed when the computer runs it.
fact: A will or a contract is executed when it is signed and made official.
fact: «Executed» can also mean a person was put to death as an official punishment by law. This is a serious, adult meaning, so ask an adult if you meet it in a book.
fact: The verb forms are execute, executes, executed and executing. Executed is the past form, so it describes something that has already happened.
exercise: «The gymnast executed a perfect somersault.» What does executed mean here? | Lost or hidden | Broke into pieces | Painted in bright colours | *Carried out well
exercise: The teacher says, «The program is executed when you press Run.» What does executed mean? | Thrown away | Forgotten by the computer | Painted in bright colours | *Run by the computer
exercise: «Ben executed every step of the dance without a single mistake.» Which word tells you Ben did it fully and well? | step | mistake | every | *executed
test: «The team executed their plan, and they scored three goals.» What does executed mean here? | Hidden from the other team | *Carried out or done | Thrown away | Made quieter
test: Lily says executed must mean hanged, because it sounds scary. What is a better way to check? | Ask the nearest dog | Guess and move on without checking | *Read the words around it and see which meaning fits | Look only at the first letter
exam: «The judge said the contract was executed once both people had signed it.» What does executed mean here? | Written in pencil | *Signed and made official | Loudly announced in the street | Torn up and thrown away
